From 9283571760ffd3a4af7d39b08ae61f8457836f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kasniya <36neelansh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:58:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(decorate): biome-gate lush cave scans; one read per scan
 step and face test; cache patch ground tests

- placement: a placed chain whose biome filter is preceded by draw-free, column-keeping,
  non-tallying modifiers (environment_scan, constant y-only random_offset, ...) drops a
  center-chunk position before that run when no quart of its 4x4 column has a biome listing
  the feature (DecorationRegion::center_biome_columns). The skipped run neither draws nor
  writes nor tallies, so output is unchanged.
- environment_scan with local predicates reads each position once (DecorationRegion::probe)
  and caches (allowed, target) per StateKey within the scan.
- face_full answers every fact from one probe and asks only the facts it needs.
- vegetation_patch: the air walks reuse the last answer instead of re-reading; a constant
  ground state is interned on its first landing write, and the name/replaceable tests are
  cached per StateKey; flood water is interned on first landing write.

Random draws, write order and state-table order are unchanged; pregen digest df701ee858e2bdd3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
